finding: Blocking — src/engine/app/index.ts:439-445 (contract at 421-422): world-less cleanup observes only the global document. A connected canvas parent inside a ShadowRoot satisfies the stated mounting precondition, but removing its overlay or an ancestor inside that root produces no mutation on document (subtree does not cross shadow boundaries). Both observers therefore remain live indefinitely unless some unrelated light-DOM mutation later happens. The document observer retains the closure/overlay and the resize observer continues observing the canvas, so repeated mounts/removals accumulate retained overlays. The light-DOM-only removal fixtures at src/engine/app/browser/overlay.e2e.ts:9-35 cannot catch this. Honor removal in the mounted tree, or explicitly bound the new public lifetime promise to the supported tree; add a failing control for that boundary. This is a static DOM-semantics counterexample, not a newly executed browser reproduction. The recorded Chromium scale checks and final validation order otherwise satisfy the stage's enumerated Check; enlarged pointer-driven slider interaction remains unproved by the existing fill-based hud test.
